        "whenNotToUse": "Do not confuse with 'call forwarding'. Call forwarding is an end-user action redirecting one individual line to a mobile phone; call routing is an automated enterprise architecture distributing organizational calls across multiple endpoints.",
        "whenToUse": "Use when discussing telecommunications setup, customer service operations, VoIP phone system capabilities, switchboard management, or contact center workflows."
