        "commonMistakes": "Learners frequently stress the first or third syllable of 'committee' (saying /\u02c8k\u0252m.\u026a.ti\u02d0/ or /k\u0259.m\u026a\u02c8ti\u02d0/); the correct stress is firmly on the second syllable /k\u0259\u02c8m\u026at.i/. Additionally, in 'meeting', non-native speakers may pronounce a hard /t/ instead of an American flap /t\u032c/ (/\u02c8mi\u02d0.t\u032c\u026a\u014b/) or reduce the final /-\u026a\u014b/ to /-\u026an/.",
