        "howNativesThink": "To a native speaker, a 'committee meeting' conveys formal governance, strict adherence to agendas, procedural rules (like Robert's Rules of Order), and collective accountability. Unlike an informal team check-in or brainstorm, a committee meeting has a designated chair, recorded minutes, formal motions, and a specific charter (such as audit, steering, ethics, or safety). Native professionals often associate it with structured debate, voting, and formal reporting back to an overarching board.",
        "mentalImage": "A group of eight departmental directors seated around a mahogany conference table with printed committee dossiers, laptops open to financial spreadsheets, a gavel beside the committee chair at the head of the table, and an administrative secretary recording minutes on a stenographic tablet.",
