        "howNativesThink": "To a native IT manager or business administrator, a 'database backup' represents non-negotiable operational insurance. It carries an aura of preparedness and disaster avoidance. When system errors occur, the immediate instinctive question is always, 'When was the last database backup run?' It is viewed not as a casual file copy, but as an intact structural replica capable of preventing corporate collapse.",
