        "howNativesThink": "To a native administrative worker, a 'date stamp' represents indisputable proof of receipt. It turns an ordinary paper document into an authenticated, timestamped record for audit and compliance purposes. Applying a date stamp establishes the exact legal moment an organization accepted a document, protecting against disputes regarding submission deadlines, payment discounts, or delivery delays. It evokes the familiar mechanical clack-thunk sound of a spring-loaded dater hitting an intake desk blotter.",
