        "howNativesThink": "To native corporate professionals and legal officers, a 'digital signature' is fundamentally distinct from an 'electronic signature' or a pasted JPEG image of handwriting. Natives immediately perceive it as a secure, audit-proof cryptographic lock backed by a trusted Certificate Authority (CA) that guarantees non-repudiation in court. It represents modern speed and compliance, eliminating the archaic logistical friction of printing, ink-signing, scanning, and courier mailing.",
