        "howNativesThink": "To native speakers in professional environments, a 'direct telephone line' is a mark of accessibility, seniority, and mutual respect. Rather than forcing an important client or business partner to wade through automated phone trees ('Press 1 for Sales...') or wait on hold with a receptionist, giving someone your direct telephone line says: 'Your time is valuable; reach me straight at my desk.' It conveys an open channel of communication devoid of bureaucratic gatekeeping.",
