        "evolution": "In Medieval Latin, a 'dispensator' was a steward who disbursed rations or funds. In the industrial manufacturing boom of the early 20th century, consumable office and packaging goods\u2014such as 3M Scotch cellophane tape (1930) and perforated paper toweling\u2014began being wound around standardized hollow cores designed specifically to fit onto the spindles of desktop dispensers or wall brackets. The compound 'dispenser roll' became standard in office stationery procurement and janitorial supply catalogs to differentiate spool-mounted continuous refills from flat, cut sheets.",
