        "culturalContext": "In commercial office administration and facilities management across English-speaking countries, standardizing dispenser roll dimensions (e.g., standard 1-inch and 3-inch tape cores, universal paper towel rolls) is an essential cost-control measure that prevents offices from buying proprietary refills that don't fit existing hardware. In TOEIC Part 1, office and warehouse photographs frequently show workers packaging boxes using handheld tape dispensers or restocking rolls.",
