        "howNativesThink": "Native speakers view the 'emergency exit sign' as an essential, non-negotiable life-safety safeguard rather than ordinary interior decor. It immediately conjures vivid associations of glowing red or green illumination penetrating a darkened or smoke-filled corridor, routine building fire drills, and strict regulatory inspections by the local fire marshal.",
