        "howNativesThink": "To native speakers, an 'errand runner' is a pragmatic and indispensable administrative support role that protects executive and professional productivity. While colloquial terms like 'go-fer' (from 'go for this, go for that') can occasionally sound dismissive, 'errand runner' is an objective, functional descriptor. Natives associate the role with someone trustworthy, resourceful, punctual, and adept at navigating urban transit, building security protocols, and strict municipal deadlines.",
