        "exampleQuestion": "If front-line representatives cannot resolve a billing discrepancy within twenty-four hours, they are required to follow the established ______ path and notify a regional supervisor. (A) escalate (B) escalates (C) escalated (D) escalation",
        "tips": "In TOEIC Part 5, test-takers are regularly tested on noun-noun compounds (where a noun functions as an adjectival modifier for another noun). In 'the established ______ path', the noun 'path' requires a modifier naming the specific business process, which is the noun 'escalation' (D). Choice (A) 'escalate' is a base verb, (B) 'escalates' is a third-person singular verb, and (C) 'escalated' is a past participle/adjective (which would illogically mean that the path itself was intensified). In Part 7 reading passages, corporate policy manuals and customer service guidelines frequently detail tiered escalation paths."
