        "howNativesThink": "Native speakers use \"executive suite\" in two distinct but related ways: spatially (the physical top floor where senior management works) and metonymically (the high-level leadership body that makes company-wide decisions). Saying \"a memo came down from the executive suite\" signals that the decision is definitive and carries the highest institutional authority. In corporate journalism, \"trouble in the executive suite\" immediately conveys internal power struggles among the CEO, CFO, and board.",
        "mentalImage": "Frosted double glass doors with brushed metal handles sliding open on the 50th floor to reveal an expansive walnut-paneled reception area, a receptionist behind a marble console, and corridors lined with senior officers' offices offering panoramic city vistas.",
        "whenNotToUse": "Do not use to describe general employee cubicle floors, departmental bullpen areas, single isolated cubicles, or middle-management shared offices (use \"operations floor\", \"open office\", or \"departmental office\").",
