        "howNativesThink": "To an experienced office administrator, corporate controller, or records manager, a 'forms inventory' represents strict procedural discipline. Native speakers understand that running out of a vital form (like a customs declaration, tax withholding form, or surgical consent waiver) or circulating an obsolete version with outdated legal boilerplate exposes the enterprise to severe operational delays or regulatory fines. Therefore, a forms inventory is viewed both as a physical supply tally and an active version-control safeguard.",
