        "culturalContext": "A cornerstone of 20th and 21st-century Western office administration. Brands like Pendaflex became household names in North America. Even in the digital era, law firms, healthcare facilities, accounting departments, and government agencies maintain extensive hanging file drawer banks for physical compliance, wet-ink contracts, and vital records.",
        "howNativesThink": "Native office workers distinguish sharply between an ordinary 'folder' (a Manila tabbed jacket that you carry in your hands or tuck into a briefcase) and a 'hanging folder' (the sturdy green suspension pocket that lives permanently inside a metal cabinet drawer). Natives think of hanging folders as the skeletal framework of an analog filing system: you drop Manila folders inside them, and you attach clear plastic angled tabs with white label inserts to their slotted tops so you can visually scan an alphabetized drawer in seconds. Mentioning hanging folders evokes images of opening a deep, ball-bearing filing cabinet drawer that glides smoothly open.",
