        "howNativesThink": "Native English speakers associate a highlighter pen with critical reading, proofreading, and contract analysis. Unlike an opaque felt-tip marker, a highlighter is strictly transparent\u2014its sole function is to draw the reader's eye to vital terms, deadlines, or monetary figures without defacing the legibility of the page.",
        "mentalImage": "An administrative assistant running a vibrant neon-yellow chisel-tipped marker across the liability clause of an agreement, creating an even, semi-transparent luminous band over the black typography.",
        "whenNotToUse": "Do not use when referring to digital annotation tools unless specifying 'digital highlighter', and avoid confusing it with an indelible permanent marker (Sharpie) or dry-erase whiteboard marker.",
