        "howNativesThink": "To native administrative and accounting professionals, a 'petty cash voucher' embodies internal fiscal control. No matter how small an expenditure is\u2014even a $4.50 carton of milk for the breakroom\u2014cash cannot leave the lockbox without a voucher. It serves as an audit paper trail: at the end of the month, the physical banknotes remaining plus the monetary value of all signed vouchers must balance exactly to the fund's fixed float.",
        "mentalImage": "A yellow carbonless paper slip titled 'Petty Cash Voucher' bearing filled-in entries for date, department code, $18.50 amount, purpose ('Emergency Postage Stamps'), and an authorized signature, stapled to a post office receipt next to a small metal lockbox filled with cash.",
