        "howNativesThink": "To native business executives and operational managers, a 'processing backlog' signals a red-alert operational bottleneck that threatens customer satisfaction, triggers service level agreement (SLA) penalties, and causes staff burnout. Unlike a healthy, planned 'pipeline' or 'queue', a 'backlog' implies stagnation\u2014work is entering the system faster than staff or software can clear it. Addressing a processing backlog requires managerial intervention, such as approving mandatory weekend overtime, hiring temporary data-entry contractors, or re-engineering automated workflows.",
