        "howNativesThink": "To native speakers in commerce and administration, a 'purchase order form' (commonly abbreviated as 'PO form') is not merely a piece of paper; it represents a legally enforceable commercial commitment. Once sent to and accepted by the vendor, it constitutes a binding contract. Administrative professionals emphasize three-way matching: the 'purchase order form', the 'packing slip / receiving report', and the 'vendor invoice' must all align to the penny before accounts payable releases payment.",
