        "howNativesThink": "To native speakers in corporate, legal, and financial sectors, 'record keeping' is the bedrock of corporate credibility and legal protection. It carries a strong connotation of institutional rigor and thoroughness. Native speakers instinctively view 'impeccable record keeping' as the ultimate defense against lawsuits, regulatory fines, and tax discrepancies, while 'shoddy record keeping' suggests imminent organizational peril or intentional malfeasance.",
