        "howNativesThink": "To a native speaker, a 'reminder note' is soft, collegial, and preventative. It differs significantly from an 'ultimatum' or a formal 'warning notice.' Leaving a reminder note implies good faith\u2014assuming the recipient simply forgot or has a busy schedule, rather than willful neglect. It can be a self-directed sticky note ('Buy printer toner') or a courteous nudge to a co-worker ('Friendly reminder: budget drafts due at noon').",
